  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25890172",
      "title": "Exploring the Base Types",
      "sourceHash": "b5dddd599be000c940d29a32b273295761fa4defc31a8c17c7fe52bdefb8f073",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 5.98,
          "en": "Now let's dig deeper into typescript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.98,
          "end": 9.66,
          "en": "And for this, I'll add a new basics.ts file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.66,
          "end": 13.53,
          "en": "In which we'll dive into some core basics you need to know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 13.53,
          "end": 15.22,
          "en": "about typescript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.22,
          "end": 18.81,
          "en": "And for that, I wanna start with the basic types",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.81,
          "end": 20.81,
          "en": "you can work with in typescript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.81,
          "end": 23.19,
          "en": "which you will need all the time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.19,
          "end": 25.94,
          "en": "And that will be our primitives, which we know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.94,
          "end": 30.83,
          "en": "from JavaScript, numbers, strings and booleans.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.83,
          "end": 35.3,
          "en": "And then of course, we also have more complex types",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.3,
          "end": 39.28,
          "en": "like arrays or objects, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.28,
          "end": 40.54,
          "en": "And then we're there after",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.54,
          "end": 43.44,
          "en": "we'll also talk about function types,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.44,
          "end": 45.89,
          "en": "parameters and much more.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.89,
          "end": 49.66,
          "en": "So that's generally what I wanna talk about here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.66,
          "end": 52.693,
          "en": "And let's start with the primitives here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.57,
          "end": 55.58,
          "en": "The primitive values we have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.58,
          "end": 59.45,
          "en": "in JavaScript are numbers, strings, booleans",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.45,
          "end": 62.96,
          "en": "and also a null and undefined and also symbols.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.96,
          "end": 64.08,
          "en": "But we can ignore that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.08,
          "end": 67.82,
          "en": "And number, string and boolean as well as null and undefined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.82,
          "end": 70.11,
          "en": "are the important ones therefore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.11,
          "end": 73.07,
          "en": "Now if we have a variable, let's say, let's say the age",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.07,
          "end": 75.66,
          "en": "of a user, and we wanna make it cleater,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.66,
          "end": 78.03999999999999,
          "en": "that India we wanna have a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.03999999999999,
          "end": 81.33,
          "en": "We can make that clarification with typescript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.33,
          "end": 84.57,
          "en": "by adding a colon after the variable name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.57,
          "end": 87.157,
          "en": "and then simply specifying the type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.157,
          "end": 90.58,
          "en": "of value that should be stored in this variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.58,
          "end": 94.37,
          "en": "And then we can finish this variable declaration here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.37,
          "end": 98.72999999999999,
          "en": "If I then later assign a value, assigning a number is okay",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.72999999999999,
          "end": 103.05,
          "en": "including floats, so numbers with a decimal place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.05,
          "end": 106.81,
          "en": "but assigning a string would give me an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.81,
          "end": 108.16,
          "en": "That's what we saw before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108.16,
          "end": 110.85300000000001,
          "en": "with that function and its parameters as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 112.28,
          "end": 115.32,
          "en": "Now, of course, we can also assign a value here right away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 115.32,
          "end": 118.07,
          "en": "We don't have to have this declaration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 118.07,
          "end": 119.87,
          "en": "without a value assignment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 119.87,
          "end": 121.163,
          "en": "Both is allowed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.88,
          "end": 125.79,
          "en": "Now we also can of course have a username",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 125.79,
          "end": 127.1,
          "en": "which should be a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 127.1,
          "end": 129.93,
          "en": "And for that, we can assign a type like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 129.93,
          "end": 133.4,
          "en": "String is the type we wanna use here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 133.4,
          "end": 135.45,
          "en": "And one important note here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 135.45,
          "end": 139.9,
          "en": "in typescript it's number and string written like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 139.9,
          "end": 142.53,
          "en": "with lower case starting characters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 142.53,
          "end": 144.87,
          "en": "It's not number like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 144.87,
          "end": 146.96,
          "en": "We don't get an error if we use that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 146.96,
          "end": 151.51,
          "en": "but this actually points at the number object in JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 151.51,
          "end": 154.24,
          "en": "We want the number primitive type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 154.24,
          "end": 158.17000000000002,
          "en": "which starts with a lowercase N, the same for string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 158.17000000000002,
          "end": 160.11,
          "en": "We want the primitive type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 160.11,
          "end": 162.82,
          "en": "which starts with a lowercase S",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 162.82,
          "end": 165.413,
          "en": "and then of course, here we can assign a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 166.41,
          "end": 167.67000000000002,
          "en": "And we can also of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 167.67000000000002,
          "end": 172.4,
          "en": "store boolean values like is instructor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 173.82999999999998,
          "end": 178.38,
          "en": "and add boolean as a type assignment so that their after,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 178.38,
          "end": 182.23,
          "en": "I may store true or false in that variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 182.23,
          "end": 185.52,
          "en": "And these are our core primitive value types",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 185.52,
          "end": 188.86,
          "en": "which we can assign, in this case to variables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 188.86,
          "end": 193.4,
          "en": "before we also saw how we set types for function parameters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 193.4,
          "end": 197.63,
          "en": "And we'll see more places where we can set types",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 197.63,
          "end": 199.023,
          "en": "in the next minutes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 200.15,
          "end": 203.36,
          "en": "Now, as I mentioned, we also have null and undefined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 203.36,
          "end": 208.36,
          "en": "as types, but we don't typically set something to be null.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 208.55,
          "end": 213.55,
          "en": "If I set hobbies to null here, then this would be possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 215.03,
          "end": 218.26,
          "en": "But then whenever I try to assign anything, I get an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 218.26,
          "end": 220.95,
          "en": "which of course is not too useful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 220.95,
          "end": 222.64,
          "en": "Instead we'll use null",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 222.64,
          "end": 225.5,
          "en": "and undefined in a slightly different way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 225.5,
          "end": 227.94,
          "en": "which we'll learn about in a couple of minutes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 227.94,
          "end": 229.82,
          "en": "So number, strings and booleans,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 229.82,
          "end": 233.583,
          "en": "are the core primitive value types we should be aware of.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}